{"id": "EUVD-2026-60095", "enisaUuid": "3f698e7c-af15-3a32-986b-7d5f3d75fe02", "description": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.0 contain a vulnerability in PublicKeyBundle.from_dict() that creates key bundles from untrusted data without verifying signatures. Attackers can call from_dict() followed by to_identity() without signature verification to encrypt data using attacker-controlled public keys, leaking secrets.", "datePublished": "2026-08-17T11:04:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:24:49", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jahlives/openssl_encrypt/security/advisories/GHSA-8h88-gxp3-j7pg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openssl-encrypt-before-unverified-key-bundle-encryption"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74876", "GHSA-723w-crw6-p9hx", "PYSEC-2026-3756"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4945329b-cc97-3a17-8293-d4c54f839f25", "product": {"name": "openssl_encrypt", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "01431b00-a068-32b9-9193-4ca787cdde20", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}], "isExploited": false}